  ('8dac645a-4338-4a9c-87fa-6e6609540960', '4467712389', 'SAP SD Consultant- only English needed', 'We are partnering with a successful international organisation seeking an experienced SAP SD Consultant to join their in-house SAP team in Vienna.

This position offers an excellent opportunity for a strong SAP SD professional who enjoys being hands-on while having opportunity to grow in a Lead role in the future. You will play a key role in SAP projects, process improvements, and operational support, with the opportunity to take on increasing responsibility for coordinating and mentoring team members over time.

Key points: In-house | Permanent | SAP SD | Fluent English | Vienna-based | Hybrid Working

Your Responsibilities

Lead and support international SAP SD implementation and rollout projects
Analyse, design, and optimise end-to-end Sales & Distribution processes
Drive continuous improvements across the SAP SD landscape
Support business users and local subsidiaries across multiple countries
Manage and resolve incidents, change requests, and operational issues
Collaborate closely with business stakeholders and cross-functional SAP teams
Support integration between SD and other SAP modules, including MM, FI, and Logistics
Perform complex troubleshooting and debugging activities
Deliver user training and knowledge transfer sessions in English
Act as a trusted advisor to the business and contribute to SAP roadmap discussions
Take on increasing leadership responsibilities, with the potential to develop into a Team Lead position

Your Profile

Degree in Business Administration, Business Informatics, Information Technology, or a related discipline
Minimum 5 years of hands-on SAP SD consulting experience
Strong understanding of end-to-end Order-to-Cash processes
Experience with SAP implementations, rollouts, or transformation projects
Strong debugging and troubleshooting skills
Excellent analytical and problem-solving abilities
Proactive, organised, and solution-oriented approach
Ability to coordinate stakeholders and influence outcomes across teams
Previous mentoring, coaching, or informal leadership experience would be advantageous
Fluent English
Willingness to travel internationally (up to 20%)
Must be eligible to work in Austria

Nice to Have

Experience with additional SAP Logistics modules
ABAP debugging knowledge
Previous experience acting as a key user, stream lead, or project lead
Experience working in international SAP environments

What''s in it for You?

Join a well-established and financially stable international organisation
Work on large-scale international SAP projects and rollouts
Potential to grow into a Lead role
Collaborative and supportive working environment
Hybrid working model based in Vienna
Long-term career development opportunities
Opportunity to shape business-critical processes and solutions

Interested?

If you''re an experienced SAP SD Consultant looking for the next step in your career, we''d love to hear from you. Apply today for a confidential discussion.
