  ('3051e9d2-84be-4c22-8bbc-c39c03cbd918', '4d7d0f4d-cfdd-45a8-9639-cf22b7fad827', 'Technical Solution Architect (m/f/d) SAP S/4HANA', 'Date: Sep 9, 2026

Location:

Weinheim, BW, DE, 69469

Functional Area: Remote

Syntax is a leading Managed Cloud Provider for Mission Critical Enterprise Applications and has been providing comprehensive technology solutions to businesses of all sizes since 1972. Syntax has undisputed strength to implement and manage ERP deployments (Oracle, SAP) in a secure and resilient private, public or hybrid cloud. With strong technical and functional consulting services, and world-class monitoring and automation, Syntax serves some of North America’s largest corporations across a diverse range of industries. Syntax has offices worldwide, and partners with Oracle, SAP, AWS, Microsoft, IBM and other global technology leaders.

Remote, hybrid, or at our office in Weinheim 

Would you like to actively build up the SAP technology sector in Europe and develop innovative solutions that sustainably increase our customers'' business success? Then become an SAP S/4HANA Technical Solution Architect (m/f/d) at Syntax and take on a key role in our customers'' transformation to S/4HANA. With over 40 years of experience and a global presence, we offer you the opportunity to lead projects using state-of-the-art technologies and apply your expertise as an industry leader.

Your Responsibilities

MOVE to S/4HANA

SAP RISE & SAP GROW transformation to the SAP cloud
S/4HANA brownfield transformation
S/4HANA bluefield transformation (SNP tools)
S/4HANA Green Field Transformation
Hybrid SAP System Landscapes
Business Technology Platform (BTP) Implementation
FIORI Enablement for S/4HANA On Premise and S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition
Data Migration Planning
Data Transformation for Carve-In or Carve-Out Projects

Architecture and Innovation – Developing Future-Proof Solutions

Analysis of current business requirements and definition of technological goals
Creation, design, and implementation of customized SAP solutions that are perfectly aligned with our customers'' corporate strategy
Identification and communication of risks (business, technical, application-related) at the corporate and business level
Participation in business and architecture planning meetings to anticipate future strategies
Definition of rollout, release, and deployment strategies, as well as support in planning project scope, schedules, and responsibilities

Customer support from pre-sales to go-live and, if necessary, transfer to AMS

Collaboration with pre-sales in finding solutions
Feasibility analysis and clarification of technical framework conditions for a project with customers, if necessary, syntax infrastructure, Basis, SAP, partners, and developers
Preparation and management of customer presentations and site assessments
Collaboration with project management in planning and selecting any necessary special resources
Coordination of cut-over plans and support during go-live
Transfer of the new system to AMS (for new and existing customers) 

Integration and coordination – successfully implementing projects

Coordinating and managing interdisciplinary teams (consultants, developers, analysts) across all project phases: analysis, design, configuration, development, testing, documentation, and production handover.
Ensuring the integrity and end-to-end integration of all solution components.
Supporting fit-to-standard workshops, validating technical solutions, and identifying process improvements.
Diagnosing and solving complex SAP problems as quickly as possible during projects.
Designing and architecting new SAP landscapes that are scalable, cost-efficient, and future-proof.

Your profile

A degree in computer science, information technology, software engineering, integrated standard software in business, or comparable training
At least 15 years of experience in SAP implementations, particularly with SAP S/4HANA transformations and carve-in/out projects, technical development expertise
Basic knowledge of the various functional areas of SAP ERP & S/4HANA
Experience with the implementation of various SAP and partner solutions
Basic knowledge of the SAP Basis environment and network infrastructure
Expertise in pre-sales activities, blueprints, explore/fit-to-standard processes, and integration projects
Strong strategic and tactical skills with excellent planning and implementation abilities
Excellent verbal and written communication skills in German and English (required for working with international customers and partners)
Ability to address objections confidently and persuasively, as well as a high degree of discipline in customer interactions

Why Syntax?

Become a part of our success story and work in a company with exciting innovation projects that are causing a stir across the industry. We recently launched one of the world''s most advanced manufacturing facilities based on SAP S/4HANA Cloud and SAP Digital Manufacturing Cloud for Execution - for Smart Press Shop, a pioneering joint venture between Porsche and forming specialist Schuler.

Competitive, above-average compensation
Global tourist: With us, you can also work from abroad from time to time
Flexible working time models, home office
Attractive benefits, e.g. company pension scheme or various health offers
A modern environment in which the "you" is part of it
Open feedback culture, flat hierarchies and a motivated team
