  ('310433ec-00ac-44fe-bc94-117d7b83a68f', 'cd9f1e51-b988-4cf3-b5c6-397150660178', 'Solution Architect (m/f/d) SAP Finance', 'Date: Sep 9, 2026

Location:

Weinheim, BW, DE, 69469

Functional Area: Remote

Syntax is a leading Managed Cloud Provider for Mission Critical Enterprise Applications and has been providing comprehensive technology solutions to businesses of all sizes since 1972. Syntax has undisputed strength to implement and manage ERP deployments (Oracle, SAP) in a secure and resilient private, public or hybrid cloud. With strong technical and functional consulting services, and world-class monitoring and automation, Syntax serves some of North America’s largest corporations across a diverse range of industries. Syntax has offices worldwide, and partners with Oracle, SAP, AWS, Microsoft, IBM and other global technology leaders.

Remote, hybrid, or at our office in Weinheim 

Would you like to help companies redesign and optimize their financial processes as part of S/4HANA transformations? As a Solution Architect SAP FI, you will advise our clients on the analysis, harmonization, and further development of core financial processes and play a key role in transformation and implementation projects. In doing so, you combine a deep understanding of finance processes with SAP expertise and work closely with business units, IT teams, and project stakeholders.

Your Responsibilities

Advising our clients on the design and optimization of end-to-end finance processes (e.g., Record-to-Report, Plan-to-Perform, Treasury, Group Reporting) in the SAP environment
Analyzing existing finance process landscapes and identifying opportunities for optimization, standardization, and automation
Designing, documenting, and further developing standard processes based on SAP best practices (S/4HANA Finance)
Supporting the design of global process and system landscapes (e.g., Central Finance, shared-service models, intercompany processes)
Coordinating between business units, IT, and project teams in implementation, rollout, and transformation projects
Ensuring process governance, documentation, and compliance with defined standards
Actively participating in S/4HANA transformations (Greenfield, Brownfield, Selective Data Transition)
Contribute to testing concepts, cutover planning, and hypercare phases, as well as training and change management activities
Work closely with solution architects, application consultants, and finance stakeholders to ensure end-to-end process integration

Your Profile

Bachelor’s or master’s degree in Business Informatics, Business Administration, Computer Science, or a comparable qualification
Several years of experience (approx. 10+ years) in SAP Finance process consulting (e.g., FI, CO, TRM, Group Reporting, PS, PSM)
In-depth understanding of core financial processes and corporate management (Accounting, Controlling, Consolidation, Treasury, Reporting)
Experience in S/4HANA Finance implementations or transition projects
Knowledge of modern SAP technologies and platforms such as SAP BTP, Fiori, SAP Cloud ALM, SAP Analytics Cloud, or Central Finance
Experience in process modeling and working with tools such as Signavio, ARIS, or BPMN
Strong communication and facilitation skills, as well as a confident demeanor when interacting with business units and management
Excellent written and spoken German and English skills

Why Syntax?

Become a part of our success story and work in a company with exciting innovation projects that are causing a stir across the industry. We recently launched one of the world''s most advanced manufacturing facilities based on SAP S/4HANA Cloud and SAP Digital Manufacturing Cloud for Execution - for Smart Press Shop, a pioneering joint venture between Porsche and forming specialist Schuler.

Competitive, above-average compensation
Global tourist: With us, you can also work from abroad from time to time
Flexible working time models, home office
Attractive benefits, e.g. company pension scheme or various health offers
A modern environment in which the "you" is part of it
Open feedback culture, flat hierarchies and a motivated team
Individual career planning with continuous training and coaching on the job

