Methodology: Expertise in process improvement (e.g., optimizing mass activity runs or billing cycles).
Leadership: Strong communication skills to manage stakeholders across both Finance and Operations.
Resilience: Proven ability in Risk Assessment and Change Leadership within large-scale, mission-critical SAP environments.

Required Skills & Qualifications

5+ years experience as a SAP IS‑U Consultant.
Strong knowledge of IS-U Billing (Rates, Schemas, RTP), and FI‑CA.
Understanding of utilities business processes (electricity, gas).
Familiarity with IDE/IDEXPF (market communication)
Ability to debug ABAP (reading logs/traces; coding not required).
Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities.
Excellent communication skills and stakeholder engagement.

Preferred (Nice-to-Have)

Experience with S/4HANA for Utilities, particularly S/4 FI‑CA migration.
Knowledge of AMI / Smart Metering processes.

