  ('62f69845-97fe-4050-8e70-c22d17bfdd18', '101c0343-5c7b-41d6-ac01-66e568928e9e', 'Senior SAP R2R Consultant', 'About Atos Group

Atos Group is a global leader in digital transformation with c. 56,000 employees and annual revenue of c. €7.2 billion (at the go-forward perimeter), operating in 54 countries under two brands - Atos for services and Eviden for products and systems. European number one in cybersecurity and a leader in cloud, Atos Group is committed to a secure and decarbonized future and provides tailored AI-powered, end-to-end solutions for all industries. Atos Group is the brand under which Atos SE (Societas Europaea) operates. Atos SE listed on Euronext Paris.

The purpose of Atos Group is to help design the future of the information space. Its expertise and services support the development of knowledge, education and research in a multicultural approach and contribute to the development of scientific and technological excellence. Across the world, the Group enables its customers and employees, and members of societies at large to live, work and develop sustainably, in a safe and secure information space.

We are looking for an experienced Senior SAP R2R Consultant to support SAP S/4HANA transformation programmes and drive Finance process excellence across global organisations.

As a key member of the SAP delivery team, you will be responsible for designing and implementing end-to-end Record-to-Report (R2R) solutions, collaborating with business stakeholders and cross-functional teams throughout all project phases, from solution design to go-live and hypercare support.

Key Responsibilities

SAP R2R Solution Delivery

Lead the Record-to-Report (R2R) workstream in SAP S/4HANA implementations.
Design and implement SAP Best Practice Finance processes.
Facilitate fit-to-standard workshops and business process design sessions.
Ensure compliance with SAP Clean Core principles.
Drive Finance process transformation and optimisation initiatives.


Cross-Functional Integration

Collaborate with Procure-to-Pay (P2P), Order-to-Cash (O2C), Supply Chain and Analytics teams.
Support end-to-end process integration design.
Work closely with Data Migration, SAP Fiori and Security teams.
Support integration with external applications and third-party solutions.


Testing, Deployment & Support

Support system integration testing (SIT) and user acceptance testing (UAT).
Validate solution quality and resolve process-related issues.
Support cutover planning and deployment activities.
Provide go-live and hypercare support.


Required Experience

Minimum 5 years of SAP project experience.
Proven experience in SAP S/4HANA Finance implementations.
Experience in SAP S/4HANA Private Cloud / Private Edition projects.
Participation in at least one full lifecycle SAP implementation as a Lead or Senior Consultant.
Strong understanding of SAP Activate methodology and SAP Best Practices.
Solid understanding of SAP Clean Core principles.
Deep knowledge of Record-to-Report business processes.
Experience working in international project environments.
Strong stakeholder management and communication skills.
Fluent English.


