  ('3a00ff2e-9247-4d5f-9e1c-54e17120dd5a', '86aa6218-644d-4dea-9488-6800435c0587', 'SAP FICO Partner', 'We are looking for an experienced SAP FI/CO Partner to join a highly successful consulting company specializing in SAP Supply Chain and SAP Logistics. 
As an SAP FI/CO Partner, you will play a key role in shaping the growth and strategic direction of our SAP Finance practice. You will combine your deep SAP Finance expertise with strong commercial and leadership skills, developing long-term relationships with national and international clients and identifying new business opportunities. 
You will have a high degree of autonomy to develop your own market strategy, shape our service portfolio, explore emerging technologies such as AI, and build a successful long-term career with us. 
We offer an attractive Partner-level compensation package, including a company car and many additional benefits. You can also work flexibly from home. 

Your responsibilities as an SAP FI/CO Partner: 
Take strategic responsibility for the development and growth of our SAP FI/CO consulting business.
Advise C-level executives and senior stakeholders at national and international clients on SAP Finance transformation, S/4HANA migration and business process optimization.
Develop and maintain long-term relationships with key clients and act as a trusted strategic advisor.
Identify, develop and win new business opportunities, from initial client discussions through to successful contract closure.
Shape and expand our SAP Finance service portfolio, methodologies and market proposition.
Lead and oversee complex SAP FI/CO transformation programs and ensure successful delivery together with project and delivery teams.
Develop innovative SAP Finance solutions and incorporate emerging technologies, including AI and intelligent automation, into our consulting offering.
Take responsibility for proposals, solution concepts, commercial offerings and contract negotiations.
Build, mentor and develop high-performing SAP Finance consultants and future leaders.
Contribute to the strategic development of the wider consulting organization and actively support our growth.
Represent the company at client meetings, industry events and relevant professional networks.
Through coaching and leadership, support the professional and personal development of our consultants. 
Your skills and experience: 
8+ years of SAP FI/CO consulting experience, ideally with significant experience in SAP S/4HANA transformation programs.
Proven track record of building and developing client relationships and generating consulting business.
Strong experience advising senior management and C-level stakeholders.
