  ('1baff38b-19fd-4511-8bdc-cf07573ee9c9', '92ce5f65-5fe2-4ea9-99b0-5dd74ec4d48d', 'SAP FI/CO Lead | S/4HANA Transformations | Prague', 'Are you passionate about helping businesses modernize their finance landscape with SAP S/4HANA?

We''re looking for an experienced SAP FI/CO Lead to join our client''s team, delivering complex ERP transformation projects across a variety of industries. In this role, you''ll combine your functional expertise with stakeholder management and consulting skills to design solutions that create real business value.

JOB DESCRIPTION
Take ownership of the Finance domain during SAP S/4HANA implementation and transformation projects.
Partner with business stakeholders to understand processes and translate business needs into scalable SAP FI/CO solutions.
Configure and optimize SAP Finance solutions in line with industry standards and Clean Core principles.
Lead workshops, prepare functional specifications, and support solution design.
Coordinate closely with technical teams, integration specialists, and business representatives throughout project delivery.
Share your expertise by mentoring colleagues and contributing to the development of the SAP Finance practice.
Support business development activities by participating in solution design and client presentations when needed.
CANDIDATE PROFILE
5+ years of experience working with SAP FI/CO in a consulting or project environment.
Proven involvement in SAP S/4HANA projects, including at least 2 years of hands-on experience.
Strong knowledge of Finance (FI), Controlling (CO), or both.
Experience delivering full-cycle SAP implementation or transformation projects.
Understanding of SAP integrations and overall solution architecture.
Additional experience with Treasury, Financial Supply Chain Management (FSCM), Central Finance, or other SAP Financials modules is an advantage.
Familiarity with Czech or Slovak financial legislation, including VAT, Intrastat, and local accounting practices.
Excellent analytical thinking, communication, and stakeholder management skills.
Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within international project teams.
University degree in Finance, Business, Economics, Information Technology, or a related field is welcomed.
Professional proficiency in English together with Czech or Slovak.
WE OFFER
Participation in large-scale SAP S/4HANA transformation initiatives.
Challenging projects for well-known organizations across different industries.
A collaborative international environment where knowledge sharing is part of everyday work.
Opportunities to deepen your SAP expertise through certifications, training, and continuous professional development.
Hybrid working model with a Prague-based office and flexibility to work remotely.
